00:33:41,543 --> 00:33:45,725
[SPEAKER_04]: You know, I think that the value of new growth is really going underestimated in this community.

320
00:33:46,306 --> 00:33:55,171
[SPEAKER_04]: And I think it's important that we understand that if we don't see around 1.25% new growth annually, we can't even stay even with inflation.

321
00:33:55,611 --> 00:33:56,512
[SPEAKER_04]: So we're not going to get anything.

322
00:33:57,212 --> 00:34:03,796
[SPEAKER_04]: So like Councilor Caviello said, you know, we need to think of ways that we can also generate revenue that's not on the back of the taxpayer, right?

323
00:34:04,116 --> 00:34:05,978
[SPEAKER_04]: And we've seen a move away from

324
00:34:06,938 --> 00:34:09,800
[SPEAKER_04]: the public-private partnerships that we've seen in the previous administrations.

325
00:34:10,461 --> 00:34:12,542
[SPEAKER_04]: And I think that that's something that we need to also take a look at.

326
00:34:12,642 --> 00:34:14,304
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's really a function of the administration.

327
00:34:14,324 --> 00:34:15,484
[SPEAKER_04]: That's not a function of the council.

328
00:34:15,504 --> 00:34:23,190
[SPEAKER_04]: We can't mandate public-private partnerships, but I think we can highlight and accentuate how important they are and how beneficial they are to this community.

329
00:34:24,251 --> 00:34:33,378
[SPEAKER_04]: You know, when we had Leslie come in and do the basketball code over at the high school and create a public partnership through that venue, it's been great.

330
00:34:34,078 --> 00:34:38,942
[SPEAKER_04]: The public private partnerships that we've seen down at home out with the Boston glory have been great.

331
00:34:40,063 --> 00:34:42,684
[SPEAKER_04]: And we need to capitalize on those and continue to invest in those.

332
00:34:43,285 --> 00:34:52,932
[SPEAKER_04]: And I think that that's another area that we can work on what we can, you know, bring some success to this community without doing it on the back of the taxpayer.

333
00:34:55,133 --> 00:34:55,934
[SPEAKER_06]: Any further discussion.

334
00:34:58,824 --> 00:35:09,010
[SPEAKER_03]: I would make a motion that the city council submit as a joint set of budget recommendations the following and Mr. Clark you let me know if I'm speaking too fast.

335
00:35:11,412 --> 00:35:11,732
[SPEAKER_06]: You're muted.

336
