[SPEAKER_07]: I'm gonna start.

337
00:35:17,215 --> 00:35:19,156
[SPEAKER_07]: I'm gonna start transcribing as you go hang on a second.

338
00:35:20,157 --> 00:35:24,980
[SPEAKER_03]: First one would be funding and assistant city solicitor in the law department.

339
00:35:34,817 --> 00:35:40,101
[SPEAKER_03]: The second would be $50,000 for the city council to engage a zoning consultant.

340
00:35:48,747 --> 00:35:56,632
[SPEAKER_03]: Third one would be a full funding for the new elections department, including the department head position at cap 16.

341
00:36:09,648 --> 00:36:13,729
[SPEAKER_03]: Fourth would be one additional code enforcement officer.

342
00:36:13,749 --> 00:36:19,931
[SPEAKER_07]: Yep.

343
00:36:20,992 --> 00:36:24,893
[SPEAKER_03]: And five would be increase the headcount of DPW staff.

344
00:36:30,395 --> 00:36:30,735
[SPEAKER_03]: Got it.

345
00:36:32,216 --> 00:36:33,256
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's the motion.

346
00:37:05,508 --> 00:37:08,551
[SPEAKER_07]: Is there a second on that motion?

347
00:37:09,913 --> 00:37:10,954
[SPEAKER_06]: Councillor Knight has seconded.

348
00:37:11,855 --> 00:37:12,415
[SPEAKER_06]: Be assured.

349
00:37:15,498 --> 00:37:15,819
[SPEAKER_07]: Okay.

350
00:37:19,282 --> 00:37:27,311
[SPEAKER_03]: And then I would make a further motion that we submit to the city administration, the mayor, the chief of staff and the director of finance.

351
00:37:29,404 --> 00:37:36,126
